<title>INDIA: India Procter &amp; Gamble 95/96 net higher.</title>
<headline>India Procter &amp; Gamble 95/96 net higher.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit	     262.3  vs	139.9</p>
<p>    Sales		  3,662.8  vs    2,680.4</p>
<p>    Shr (in rupees)	 18.0  vs	 N.A.</p>
<p>    Div (in rupees)	  7.5  vs	 N.A.</p>
<p>    Other income	    83.3  vs	 71.8</p>
<p>    Expenditure	  3,305.9  vs    2,606.7</p>
<p>    Interest costs	  49.7  vs	 40.6</p>
<p>    Depreciation	    77.3  vs	 51.0</p>
<p>    Taxation		 177.9  vs	  5.6</p>
<p>Note: Procter &amp; Gamble, subsidiary of the U.S. consumer products giant, said it plans to upgrade the quality of all existing brands and introduce additional world class products.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom 91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
